<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Maiden Peak from Willamette Pass</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:291-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.601292" lon="-122.036453"><ele>1565.4</ele><name>Willamette Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM node 2630339680, Willamette Pass Resort lot); confidence: high; pdf_page: 292; book_elev_ft: 5128; quote: map 65: WILLAMETTE PASS 5128'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.597173" lon="-122.033710"><ele>1553.6</ele><name>PCT trailhead</name><desc>source: OSM: junction of PCT Section D and E ways, by the PCT parking east of the highway; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 292; quote: follows the PCT 3 miles from Willamette Pass, starting behind the Department of Highways shed just east of the lodge area</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.612370" lon="-122.001528"><ele>1828.7</ele><name>PCT / Maiden Lake Trail junction (Maiden Peak Saddle)</name><desc>source: OSM: west end of Maiden Lake Trail #3841 on the PCT; DEM 6000 ft; 4.1 mi along the PCT; confidence: high; pdf_page: 292; book_elev_ft: 6200; quote: skiing 4.2 miles to the Maiden Peak Saddle by way of the Rosary Lakes Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.609935" lon="-121.972198"><ele>1949.4</ele><name>Leave the Maiden Lake Trail at 6,400 ft</name><desc>source: OSM Maiden Lake Trail node where DEM first reaches 6,396 ft, 1.73 mi from the PCT (book says about 1.2); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 293; book_elev_ft: 6400; quote: Once on the Maiden Lake Trail, ski east about 1.2 miles to the 6,400-foot contour, then leave the trail and head for the summit</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.626789" lon="-121.965030"><ele>2374.9</ele><name>Maiden Peak summit</name><desc>source: OSM node 357312191 Maiden Peak; confidence: high; pdf_page: 293; book_elev_ft: 7818; quote: at 7,818 feet Maiden Peak</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Maiden Peak from Willamette Pass</name><desc>1. Willamette Pass Sno-Park -&gt; PCT trailhead: straight (medium), 0.32 mi | 2. PCT trailhead -&gt; PCT / Maiden Lake Trail junction (Maiden Peak Saddle): osm (high), 4.13 mi | 3. PCT / Maiden Lake Trail junction (Maiden Peak Saddle) -&gt; Leave the Maiden Lake Trail at 6,400 ft: osm (high), 1.73 mi | 4. Leave the Maiden Lake Trail at 6,400 ft -&gt; Maiden Peak summit: straight (medium), 1.22 mi</desc>
